SUMMARY:Science Today: Intro to Bacteria
DESCRIPTION:Today’s Topic \nBacteria are the oldest lifeforms on Earth and outnumber us even in our own bodies. Together\, we’ll learn more about what they do\, where they came from\, and how they can affect our health. \nToday’s Expert \nMelody Xiao\, PhD Candidate in Ecology at Duke University \nGo inside the globe of the SECU Daily Planet Theater for live presentations and interactive shows led by scientists and educators. Meet researchers\, witness live demonstrations\, and engage in Q&A sessions with experts. With ever-changing topics and guests\, there’s always something new and exciting to learn.
URL:https://www.naturalsciences.org/calendar/event/science-today-intro-to-bacteria/2026-08-08/
LOCATION:Nature Research Center\, 121 West Jones Street\, Raleigh\, NC\, 27601\, United States
CATEGORIES:All Ages,Meet the Scientist,SECU Daily Planet Theater,Walk-up Programs
ORGANIZER;CN="Chris%20Smith":MAILTO:christopher.smith@naturalsciences.org
